basis(List,SpectralSequencePage) -- generators of a particular degree
*********************************************************************

  * Function: *note basis: (Macaulay2Doc)basis,
  * Usage: 
        B = basis(L, E)
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
      * E, a *note spectral sequence page: SpectralSequencePage,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Degree: (Macaulay2Doc)basis, => ..., default value null, 
      * *note Limit: (Macaulay2Doc)basis, => ..., default value infinity, 
      * *note SourceRing: (Macaulay2Doc)basis, => ..., default value null, 
      * *note Strategy: (Macaulay2Doc)basis, => ..., default value null, 
      * *note Truncate: (Macaulay2Doc)basis, => ..., default value false, 
      * *note Variables: (Macaulay2Doc)basis, => ..., default value null, 
  * Outputs:
      * B, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, Note!!  The output should
        actually be a page!!;

Description
===========

Returns generators for the requested (multi)degree of the spectral sequence
page.  It is designed to extend the function *note basis: (Macaulay2Doc)basis,
which can be applied to modules, for instance.

As a specific example consider the filtered complex $K$ below, obtained by
multiplying the minimal free resolution of the rational quartic space curve by
successive powers of the irrelevant ideal.

+------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : B = QQ[a..d];                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : J = ideal vars B;                                |
|                                                      |
|o2 : Ideal of B                                       |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C = freeResolution monomialCurveIdeal(B,{1,3,4});|
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : K = filteredComplex(J,C,4);                      |
+------------------------------------------------------+

We compute the degree $0$ piece of the $E^3$ page below.

