Examples of change of rings Spectral Sequences
**********************************************

Here are some examples of change of rings spectral sequences.

Given a ring map f: R -> S, an R-module M and an R-module S, there is a
spectral sequence E with E^2_{p,q} = Tor^S_p(Tor^R_q(M,S),N) that abuts to
Tor^R_{p+q}(M,N).

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : k=QQ;                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R=k[a,b,c];                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : S=k[s,t];                                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : f = map(S,R,{s^2,s*t,t^2});                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : RingMap S <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : N = coker vars S;                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : M = coker vars R --;                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = cokernel | a b c |                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|                            1                                                |
|o6 : R-module, quotient of R                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : F := freeResolution N;                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : pushFwdF := pushFwd(f,F);                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : G := freeResolution M;                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : E := spectralSequence(filteredComplex(G) ** pushFwdF);                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : EE := spectralSequence(G ** (filteredComplex pushFwdF));               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : e = prune E;                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : ee = prune EE;                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : e^0                                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|      +------------------------------------+---------------------------------|
