minimalPresentation(SpectralSequencePage) -- a minimal presentation of a spectral sequence page
***********************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note minimalPresentation: (Macaulay2Doc)minimalPresentation,
  * Usage: 
        E = minimalPresentation e
  * Inputs:
      * e, a *note spectral sequence page: SpectralSequencePage,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Exclude: (Macaulay2Doc)minimalPresentation_lpRing_rp, => ...,
        default value {},
  * Outputs:
      * E, a *note spectral sequence page: SpectralSequencePage,, 

Description
===========

Returns a minimal presentation of the spectral sequence page.

If we fail to prune a spectral sequence then the out-put can be highly
unintelligible.

As a specific example consider the filtered complex $K$ below, obtained by
multiplying the minimal free resolution of the rational quartic space curve by
successive powers of the irrelevant ideal.

+------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : B = QQ[a..d];                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : J = ideal vars B;                                |
|                                                      |
|o2 : Ideal of B                                       |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C = freeResolution monomialCurveIdeal(B,{1,3,4});|
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : K = filteredComplex(J,C,4);                      |
+------------------------------------------------------+

Compare some pruned and non-prunded pages the spectral sequence $E$ below.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : E = spectralSequence K;                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : E^3                                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|     +-----------------------------------------------------------------------|
