spectralSequence -- construct a spectral sequence
*************************************************

  * Usage: 
        E = spectralSequence K
  * Inputs:
      * K, a *note filtered chain complex: FilteredComplex,, A filtered complex
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Prune: spectralSequence_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmPrune=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value false,
  * Outputs:
      * E, a *note spectral sequence: SpectralSequence,, 

Description
===========

This is the primitive spectral sequence constructor.

In the example below we construct a spectral sequence $E$ from the filtered
complex $K$.

+------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : B = QQ[a..d];                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : J = ideal vars B;                                |
|                                                      |
|o2 : Ideal of B                                       |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C = freeResolution monomialCurveIdeal(B,{1,3,4});|
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : K = filteredComplex(J,C,4);                      |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : E = spectralSequence K                           |
|                                                      |
|o5 = E                                                |
|                                                      |
|o5 : SpectralSequence                                 |
+------------------------------------------------------+

