SpectralSequencePage -- the type of all spectral sequence pages
***************************************************************

Description
===========

A (homological, or lower index) spectral sequence page consists of:

1. A fixed integer $r \geq 0$, the page number;

2. A sequence of modules $\{E^r_{p,q}\}$ for $p,q \in \mathbb{Z}$;

3. A collection of homomorphisms $\{d^r_{p,q}: E^r_{p,q} \rightarrow
E^r_{p-r,q+r-1}\}$ for $p,q \in \mathbb{Z}, r \geq 0$ such that $d^r_{p,q}
d^r_{p+r,q-r+1} = 0$ ;

4. A collection of isomorphisms $E^{r+1}_{p,q}  \rightarrow ker d^r_{p,q} /
image d^r_{p+r,q-r+1}$.

Alternatively a (cohomological, or upper index) spectral sequence page consists
of:

1'.  A fixed integer $r \geq 0$, the page number;

2'. A sequence of modules $\{E_r^{p,q}\}$ for $p,q \in \mathbb{Z}$;

3'. A collection of homomorphisms $\{d_r^{p,q}: E_r^{p,q} \rightarrow
E_r^{p+r,q-r+1}\}$ for $ p,q \in \mathbb{Z}, r \geq 0$ such that $d_r^{p,q}
d_r^{p-r,q+r-1} = 0$ ;

4'. A collection of isomorphisms $E_{r+1}^{p,q}  \rightarrow ker d_r^{p,q} /
image d_r^{p-r,q+r-1}$.

The type SpectralSequencePage is a data type for working with spectral
sequences and spectral sequence pages.

Caveat
======

The isomorphisms $4$ and $4$' are not explicitly part of the data type,
although they can be obtained by using the command *note homologyIsomorphism:
homologyIsomorphism,.

