  * Outputs:
      * d, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 

Description
===========

Returns the p,q th map on a (lower index) spectral sequence page.  The
relationship $D_{p,q} = D^{-p,-q}$ holds.

Consider the filtered complex $K$ below, obtained by multiplying the minimal
free resolution of the rational quartic space curve by successive powers of the
irrelevant ideal.

+------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : B = QQ[a..d];                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : J = ideal vars B;                                |
|                                                      |
|o2 : Ideal of B                                       |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C = freeResolution monomialCurveIdeal(B,{1,3,4});|
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : K = filteredComplex(J,C,4);                      |
+------------------------------------------------------+

We compute a map on the third page of the spectral sequence associated to $K$.

