The trivial fibration over the sphere with fibers the sphere
************************************************************

In this example we compute the spectral sequence associated to the trivial
fibration $\mathbb{S}^1 \rightarrow  \mathbb{S}^1 x \mathbb{S}^1 \rightarrow
\mathbb{S}^1$, where the map is given by one of the projections.  To give a
simplicial realization of this fibration we first make a simplicial complex
which gives a triangulation of $\mathbb{S}^1 \times \mathbb{S}^1$.  The
simplicial complex that we construct is the triangulation of the torus given in
Figure 6.4 of Armstrong's book Basic Topology and has 18 facets.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ/101[a00,a10,a20,a01,a11,a21,a02,a12,a22];                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : Delta = simplicialComplex {a00*a02*a10,                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = simplicialComplex | a11a12a22 a20a12a22                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : SimplicialComplex                                                       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|a02*a12*a10, a01*a02*a12, a01*a11*a12, a00*a01*a11, a00*a10*a11, a12*        |
|                                                                             |
|a21a02a22 a00a02a22 a11a21a22 a00a20a22 a01a02a12 a10a02a12 a01a11a12        |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|a10*a20, a12*a20*a22, a11*a12*a22, a11*a22*a21, a10*a11*a21,                 |
|                                                                             |
| a10a20a12 a01a21a02 a00a10a02 a10a11a21 a20a01a21 a10a20a21                 |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|a10*a21*a20, a20*a22*a00, a22*a00*a02, a21*a22*a02, a21*a02*a01, a20*a21*a01,|
|                                                                             |
|a00a01a11 a00a10a11 a00a20a01 |                                              |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|a20*a01*a00}                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

We can check that the homology of the simplicial complex $\Delta$ agrees with
that of the torus $\mathbb{S}^1 \times \mathbb{S}^1 $

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C = naiveTruncation(complex Delta,1, infinity)|
|                                                   |
|       ZZ 27       ZZ 18                           |
|o3 = (---)   <-- (---)                             |
|      101         101                              |
